Package: styloprofile
Type: Package
Title: Stylometric Features and Mahalanobis Outlier Distances
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Armand", "Surbakti", email = "actuallyarmand@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Extracts interpretable stylometric features from documents and
    measures how far a document sits from a reference distribution using a
    Cholesky-based squared Mahalanobis distance. Intended for studying whether
    machine-generated text is a statistical outlier relative to human writing,
    following the feature-based framing of Froehling and Zubiaga (2021)
    <doi:10.7717/peerj-cs.443> and the distance of Mahalanobis (1936).
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0)
Imports: Rcpp, stats
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), knitr, rmarkdown, microbenchmark
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
